{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GyqmaPai65Srm53BPKwEsA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: venv-symlink-trap-2026-09-02\n3\tdescription: \"a lane session created a `.venv` symlink in its worktree pointing at the repo's .venv; after the lane unloaded, the repo's own .venv was a self-referencing symlink (ELOOP) and integrate's post-merge intake crashed mid-mint — rebuild with python3 -m venv + requirements-dev.txt, then re-run intake_after_merge\"\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: f6261996-a17c-4531-90ae-cedb282ff370\n8\t  modified: 2026-09-02T10:28:49.634Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t2026-09-02, WI-572 merge: `.venv/bin/python` in /Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template\n12\traised `OSError: [Errno 62] Too many levels of symbolic links` because `.venv`\n13\thad become `.venv -> /Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template/.venv` (a link to\n14\titself, mtime 05:26 local). Cause: a lane session had created an untracked\n15\t`.venv` symlink in its worktree (sessions 02x of wi-572 mention \"the\n16\tpre-existing untracked .venv symlink\") to reuse the repo interpreter; how the\n17\trepo's own directory got replaced is not established (the integrator's unload\n18\tGC'd a \"clean\" worktree). The merge had landed; the post-merge intake died\n19\tafter bumping docs/id-watermark and writing two spec files uncommitted.\n20\t\n21\t**How to apply:**\n22\t- Rebuild: `rm .venv && python3 -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/python -m pip\n23\t  install -r requirements-dev.txt` (pinned; ~1 min). python3 here is 3.13.14.\n24\t- Then `git checkout -- docs/id-watermark`, delete the half-minted specs, and\n25\t  re-run `intake.intake_after_merge(root, {'WI-<n>': 'merged'}, merge^1, merge)`\n26\t  from the trunk root so the mint re-allocates the same ids.\n27\t- Before unloading a lane, check `ls -la <worktree>/.venv`: a real dir (35 MB,\n28\t  a session's own venv) can be rm'd; a SYMLINK must be unlinked with `rm`\n29\t  (never `rm -rf` through it) and reported. A candidate kit row: sessions\n30\t  must not create `.venv` in a worktree; the launcher exports the interpreter.\n31\t\n32\tSee [[supervised-loop-2026-09-01-evening-lessons]].\n33\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13e3d284-9cb2-46f5-9233-24a0a1319ae2","uuid":"fabf4fc4-2ca7-48fc-a9ac-e4f968dab06d","timestamp":"2026-09-02T11:08:16.189Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/venv-symlink-trap-2026-09-02.md","content":"---\nname: venv-symlink-trap-2026-09-02\ndescription: \"a lane session created a `.venv` symlink in its worktree pointing at the repo's .venv; after the lane unloaded, the repo's own .venv was a self-referencing symlink (ELOOP) and integrate's post-merge intake crashed mid-mint — rebuild with python3 -m venv + requirements-dev.txt, then re-run intake_after_merge\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: f6261996-a17c-4531-90ae-cedb282ff370\n  modified: 2026-09-02T10:28:49.634Z\n---\n\n2026-09-02, WI-572 merge: `.venv/bin/python` in /Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template\nraised `OSError: [Errno 62] Too many levels of symbolic links` because `.venv`\nhad become `.venv -> /Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template/.venv` (a link to\nitself, mtime 05:26 local). Cause: a lane session had created an untracked\n`.venv` symlink in its worktree (sessions 02x of wi-572 mention \"the\npre-existing untracked .venv symlink\") to reuse the repo interpreter; how the\nrepo's own directory got replaced is not established (the integrator's unload\nGC'd a \"clean\" worktree). The merge had landed; the post-merge intake died\nafter bumping docs/id-watermark and writing two spec files uncommitted.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- Rebuild: `rm .venv && python3 -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/python -m pip\n  install -r requirements-dev.txt` (pinned; ~1 min). python3 here is 3.13.14.\n- Then `git checkout -- docs/id-watermark`, delete the half-minted specs, and\n  re-run `intake.intake_after_merge(root, {'WI-<n>': 'merged'}, merge^1, merge)`\n  from the trunk root so the mint re-allocates the same ids.\n- Before unloading a lane, check `ls -la <worktree>/.venv`: a real dir (35 MB,\n  a session's own venv) can be rm'd; a SYMLINK must be unlinked with `rm`\n  (never `rm -rf` through it) and reported. A candidate kit row: sessions\n  must not create `.venv` in a worktree; the launcher exports the interpreter.\n\nSee [[supervised-loop-2026-09-01-evening-lessons]].\n","numLines":33,"startLine":1,"totalLines":33}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeeWPH4vR6jW5MsC9dX46","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MCakJb1yhxwXaTZDqNCsdD","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/venv-symlink-trap-2026-09-02.md","old_string":"See [[supervised-loop-2026-09-01-evening-lessons]].","new_string":"**Running a lane worktree WITHOUT making a `.venv` (confirmed WI-574,\n2026-09-02):** worktrees under `/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template-drive/<branch>/`\nhave no `.venv` and must not grow one — just invoke the trunk interpreter by\nabsolute path from the worktree root:\n`/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q -n auto`.\nEverything (pytest, xdist, the kit scripts) resolves fine against the worktree's\nown cwd. Caveat to expect and record honestly: the commit hook runs under\nambient `/usr/local/bin/python3`, which has no ruff, so every commit prints the\n\"A DECLARED CHECK DID NOT RUN — format\" banner. Harmless for a docs-only lane;\na lane touching Python must run `ruff format` through the trunk interpreter\nitself before committing.\n\nSee [[supervised-loop-2026-09-01-evening-lessons]]."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1309,"cache_read_input_tokens":122665,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1309},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13e3d284-9cb2-46f5-9233-24a0a1319ae2","uuid":"3730ff56-e3e7-49cb-ae9b-5fa740ba9313","request_id":"req_011CeeWPFYtkkKfBgtswkDCT"}
