{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeeWPmPG8c9s9euzJHhfL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-574 is closed on this branch.\n\n## Verdict: the WI-572 close **STANDS WITH FINDINGS** — two successors drafted\n\n**What shipped answers what the row asked for.** I checked every arm of WI-572's `## Context` at the tree, by symbol, and verified wiring at the *call site* rather than the definition:\n\n- `acceptance_record.staged_approval_acts` (:511) + `lane_approval_refusal` (:685) over `APPROVAL_ACT_CSVS` (:144, SN included), off the one shared `_spine_row_sides` walk (:422) — and `integrate._approval_act_refusal` (:1127) is actually **invoked** at `integrate.py:2425`. The snapshot half of the refusal really is worded by what the branch did (`_SNAPSHOT_ACT`, :606), which was the easiest claim to state and not do.\n- The first-approval arm (`intake._first_approval_drafts` :809) is dial-filtered at *both* ends through one `human_approves_spine` (:895) — the round-1 MAJOR's real fix, not a guard beside it. `Adjudicates` is a genuine `wi_convert` column, serialized at intake.py:1546.\n- `OUTSIDE_THE_APPROVAL_ACT` (:165) closes the bound against `baseline_snapshot.SNAPSHOTTED` rather than declaring it.\n\n**The finding is in the filing, not the code.** WI-572 named two follow-ons it deliberately didn't take, declared `Deferred open items: none`, and closed clean — so both live only in `docs/log.md` prose, which records what happened, not what's next. Neither appears anywhere in `docs/work/` or `open-items.toml`. Both verified still live:\n\n1. `tests/test_derive_stage.py:528` asserts the `docs/stage` fingerprint with **no** work-branch exemption while its commit-bar twin skips on a work branch — I saw that skip live in this session's own hook output. WI-572 predicted it would \"now greet routine lanes\" and queued nothing.\n2. `trace.py --approve modified` still renders every `Drafted` chain: `human_approves_spine` has exactly two callers (the mint, the adjudication brief) and `trace.py` is not one — so the plan's §2a \"Surfaces to the owner\" row is unsatisfied. Owner-owed, so it rides as an `open_item` cell that mints a pending OI gating its successor.\n\nBoth are drafted in `## Dispositions` (parse dry-run: two blocks, no refusal) for the merge to mint. Nothing about the WI-572 merge is reversed.\n\n**Bar, real output:** full unfiltered **3282 passed, 25 skipped in 566.57s**; smoke **1463 passed, 4 skipped in 21.93s**; budget **36.0s vs 60s → within**; `check_docs` 0 broken; `check_trajectory` clean.\n\nTwo things you should know rather than have buried:\n- This worktree has no `.venv` and I did not create one (the WI-572 incident). I ran everything through `/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template/.venv/bin/python`. But the **commit hook** runs under ambient `python3`, which has no ruff, so it printed \"A DECLARED CHECK DID NOT RUN — format\" on both commits. This row changes no Python so there was nothing for ruff to grade, but the banner is real and I've recorded it rather than papered over it.\n- I found a third, broader thing I deliberately did *not* mint: `gen_open_items.py --check` is satisfied by `Deferred open items: none`, so any fragment may name follow-ons in prose that reach no queue. Whether a named follow-on should be *required* to land in `## Dispositions` or an OI is doctrine a spot-check shouldn't settle unilaterally — it's recorded in the log fragment for a sitting."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":625,"cache_read_input_tokens":123974,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":625},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13e3d284-9cb2-46f5-9233-24a0a1319ae2","uuid":"44a26f1b-59c7-4b79-928d-ff14f4935d22","request_id":"req_011CeeWPkNVF84F4LFwv1ZY6"}
